WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.208 --> 00:00:02.544
Quick--when I ask
what an alien looks like,

00:00:02.544 --> 00:00:05.130
what's the first thing
that pops into your head?

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:06.923
Is it a deadly
endoparasatoid

00:00:06.923 --> 00:00:09.008
with two sets
of sharp teeth?

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:11.386
Or perhaps a small,
green, bipedal creature

00:00:11.386 --> 00:00:13.054
with large eyes?

00:00:13.054 --> 00:00:15.640
Regardless of whatever
you just pictured,

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:18.893
you've seen these gray
alien extraterrestrials

00:00:18.893 --> 00:00:20.311
somewhere before.

00:00:20.311 --> 00:00:22.564
Called Zeta Reticulans,
Roswell Greys,

00:00:22.564 --> 00:00:25.692
or simply Grays,
these extraterrestrials

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.694
are defined
by their humanoid forms,

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:29.446
exaggerated long limbs,

00:00:29.446 --> 00:00:32.115
large black eyes,
small noses,

00:00:32.115 --> 00:00:33.908
thin mouths,
and, of course,

00:00:33.908 --> 00:00:36.453
gray skin or gray clothing.

00:00:36.453 --> 00:00:38.705
There are mostly two types
of Grays--

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.832
the smaller drone
or lackey type

00:00:40.832 --> 00:00:43.710
and the more powerful
and intelligent Tall Grays.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.295
Grays are some
of pop culture's

00:00:45.295 --> 00:00:47.589
most recognizable
representations

00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:49.382
of extraterrestrial life.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:52.302
But where did this depiction
of extraterrestrials come from,

00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:54.846
and why are Grays the ones
mostly responsible

00:00:54.846 --> 00:00:56.598
for all the abductions?

00:00:58.016 --> 00:00:59.726
I'm Dr. Emily Zarka,

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.770
and this is "Monstrum."

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:04.105
Let's keep in mind
that supernatural abductions

00:01:04.105 --> 00:01:06.107
have long had a place
in folklore,

00:01:06.107 --> 00:01:07.650
mythology, and culture.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.360
From religious rites
to fairies,

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.112
deities to aliens,

00:01:11.112 --> 00:01:14.449
history is filled with stories
of humans being kidnapped,

00:01:14.449 --> 00:01:17.702
manipulated, and sometimes
returned to their homes.

00:01:17.702 --> 00:01:19.537
That's partially
why it's hard to say

00:01:19.537 --> 00:01:23.124
when the first so-called
alien encounter took place,

00:01:23.124 --> 00:01:25.168
though one of the first
on record

00:01:25.168 --> 00:01:27.170
emerged in 1638.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:29.214
The journals
of Governor John Winthrop

00:01:29.214 --> 00:01:31.049
of the Massachusetts Bay Colony

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:33.885
report the spottings
of various slight apparitions

00:01:33.885 --> 00:01:37.514
in the area, some accompanied
by disembodied voices.

00:01:37.514 --> 00:01:39.390
This rash of sightings
started a trend

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.768
that has continued
into the present day.

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:43.895
Most extraterrestrial
encounters

00:01:43.895 --> 00:01:46.064
appear in
the English-speaking world.

00:01:46.064 --> 00:01:48.900
The 19th century
is full of reports

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:51.194
originating
in the United States,

00:01:51.194 --> 00:01:53.780
like on January 22, 1878,

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.824
when Texas farmer
John Martin

00:01:55.824 --> 00:01:59.160
claimed he saw a flying disc
that appeared to be the size

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.162
of a saucer in the sky.

00:02:01.162 --> 00:02:04.332
A local newspaper immortalized
the story the next day.

00:02:04.332 --> 00:02:05.792
At the end
of the 19th century,

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.627
residents across California

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:11.297
reported incredibly
fast-moving mystery airships

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:14.092
about 45 to 60 meters
in size.

00:02:14.092 --> 00:02:17.137
Beginning in Sacramento
in November, 1896,

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:21.307
hundreds of witnesses reported
lighted aircraft in the sky.

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:24.853
Many heard voices or singing
emanating from the objects.

00:02:24.853 --> 00:02:27.939
One witness described it
as "cigar-shaped with wheels,

00:02:27.939 --> 00:02:29.732
piloted by two men."

00:02:29.732 --> 00:02:33.111
Similar sightings moved eastward
across 20 states

00:02:33.111 --> 00:02:35.029
over the following six months.

00:02:35.029 --> 00:02:37.782
One witness claimed
he narrowly avoided abduction

00:02:37.782 --> 00:02:40.451
while out driving his buggy
some 80 kilometers

00:02:40.451 --> 00:02:42.328
north of Stockton, California.

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:45.707
He discovered what he
determined was a crashed ship--

00:02:45.707 --> 00:02:49.669
a metallic, smooth object
roughly 45 meters long.

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:53.298
Inside were three pale,
thin, seven-feet-tall

00:02:53.298 --> 00:02:56.426
warbling creatures who tried
to force him aboard,

00:02:56.426 --> 00:02:58.219
but he resisted and fled.

00:02:58.219 --> 00:03:00.597
The shift
from fairy abduction motifs

00:03:00.597 --> 00:03:02.181
and supernatural encounters

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:05.518
to more technology-based
extraterrestrial reports

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:08.062
could be attributed
to emerging technologies

00:03:08.062 --> 00:03:10.857
and a cultural movement
away from superstition.

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:13.359
And let's not forget
that the 19th century

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.111
marked the first successful

00:03:15.111 --> 00:03:18.740
non-balloon-powered
flight crafts in human history.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:22.118
Gliders and controlled aircraft
powered by steam engines,

00:03:22.118 --> 00:03:23.494
compressed air mechanisms,

00:03:23.494 --> 00:03:25.830
and eventually
battery-powered crafts

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:29.208
were tested by governments,
scientists, and hobbyists.

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:32.587
Many of these attempts were
well-publicized. Just saying.

00:03:32.587 --> 00:03:35.924
Still, all was relatively quiet
on the alien-encounter front

00:03:35.924 --> 00:03:37.717
until the 1940s.

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:41.512
1946 to 1960 brought
another wave of sightings,

00:03:41.512 --> 00:03:44.015
this time across
the Western world,

00:03:44.015 --> 00:03:47.727
earning the period the moniker
"The Flying Saucer Era."

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:51.356
The United States, Germany,
Norway, France, Italy,

00:03:51.356 --> 00:03:55.193
and Finland saw spikes
in unusual aerial phenomenon.

00:03:55.193 --> 00:03:57.445
Most reports indicated
the appearance

00:03:57.445 --> 00:04:01.199
of either a cigar- or circular-
shaped wingless aerial craft

00:04:01.199 --> 00:04:03.076
accompanied by bright lights.

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:05.745
The press labeled
these first European sightings

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:08.998
a the "Ghost Rocket" scare
of 1946.

00:04:08.998 --> 00:04:11.751
The public and intelligence
organizations alike

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:14.545
nervously wondered
if these flying objects

00:04:14.545 --> 00:04:16.381
weren't alien craft

00:04:16.381 --> 00:04:19.342
but real missiles originating
from the Soviet Union.

00:04:19.342 --> 00:04:22.345
Cold War anxieties have long
been proposed by historians

00:04:22.345 --> 00:04:25.348
as one explanation
for increases in sightings.

00:04:25.348 --> 00:04:27.100
Other considerations?

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.894
The blossoming movie
and television industry's

00:04:29.894 --> 00:04:32.188
embracing alien mythology

00:04:32.188 --> 00:04:34.899
and the growing popularity
of the science-fiction genre

00:04:34.899 --> 00:04:36.943
across all forms of media.

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:39.737
1947 was quite the year
for alien activity.

00:04:39.737 --> 00:04:41.990
That year, U.S. pilot
Kenneth Arnold

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:45.243
observed nine objects
he said moved like a saucer

00:04:45.243 --> 00:04:47.120
being thrown across water.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.789
A newspaper reporter
misunderstood

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:51.749
and published
Arnold's description

00:04:51.749 --> 00:04:53.835
as a "flying saucer."

00:04:53.835 --> 00:04:56.421
As the news of the encounter
and term spread,

00:04:56.421 --> 00:04:58.423
so many sightings
were reported

00:04:58.423 --> 00:05:01.092
that the Air Force
opened an investigation.

00:05:01.092 --> 00:05:04.887
And July 8 is an infamous day
in alien encounter history--

00:05:04.887 --> 00:05:06.472
the Roswell Incident.

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.016
Following a press release

00:05:08.016 --> 00:05:10.059
from the official
U.S. Army Air Force,

00:05:10.059 --> 00:05:13.896
the Associated Press reported
to radio shows and newspapers

00:05:13.896 --> 00:05:16.315
that the remains
of a flying disc

00:05:16.315 --> 00:05:19.152
had been found outside
Roswell, New Mexico.

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:22.363
The U.S. military quickly
retracted its initial report

00:05:22.363 --> 00:05:25.199
in a statement from
the Roswell Army Air Field,

00:05:25.199 --> 00:05:27.493
claiming the object
was a weather balloon.

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:30.455
As unidentified aerial
phenomenon sightings increased

00:05:30.455 --> 00:05:31.956
in the '40s and '50s,

00:05:31.956 --> 00:05:34.208
so did the diversity
and frequency

00:05:34.208 --> 00:05:36.419
of aliens
in science-fiction texts.

00:05:36.419 --> 00:05:38.713
The 1950 movie
"The Flying Saucer"

00:05:38.713 --> 00:05:41.716
capitalized on the fascination
with spacecraft.

00:05:41.716 --> 00:05:44.218
Other movies like "The Day
the Earth Stood Still"

00:05:44.218 --> 00:05:46.220
portray aliens as so humanoid

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:48.973
they appear to be humans.

00:05:48.973 --> 00:05:51.768
Their technology and status
as extraterrestrials

00:05:51.768 --> 00:05:54.187
is what marks them as alien.

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:56.981
Technology in the real world
was changing as well.

00:05:56.981 --> 00:05:58.941
The first artificial
Earth satellite

00:05:58.941 --> 00:06:01.652
launched on October 4, 1957.

00:06:01.652 --> 00:06:04.113
That same year,
the Gray alien legacy

00:06:04.113 --> 00:06:06.365
begins to appear in reports.

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:08.868
Brazilian farmer
Antonio Vilas-Boas

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:10.745
claimed he saw a red star

00:06:10.745 --> 00:06:13.122
that grew brighter as
it approached him in the sky.

00:06:13.122 --> 00:06:15.792
He testified that short beings
from outer space

00:06:15.792 --> 00:06:17.210
wearing gray suits

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:18.878
took him to the spacecraft

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:21.714
and performed physical
and sexual experiments on him.

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:24.258
Gray abductions did become
a global sensation

00:06:24.258 --> 00:06:26.302
four years later
in New Hampshire

00:06:26.302 --> 00:06:28.971
on September 19, 1961.

00:06:28.971 --> 00:06:30.681
As Barney and Betty Hill

00:06:30.681 --> 00:06:32.850
were driving down
a lone stretch of dark road

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:35.019
on Highway 3
in the White Mountains,

00:06:35.019 --> 00:06:37.313
Betty noticed strange lights
in the sky

00:06:37.313 --> 00:06:40.149
that she initially mistook
for a falling star

00:06:40.149 --> 00:06:43.694
until it moved upward
and increased in intensity.

00:06:43.694 --> 00:06:45.655
The couple stopped the car
to look at the lights

00:06:45.655 --> 00:06:46.823
and walk their dog.

00:06:46.823 --> 00:06:48.533
While Barney was with the dog,

00:06:48.533 --> 00:06:50.785
Betty looked at the lights
through binoculars,

00:06:50.785 --> 00:06:53.538
and what she saw
shocked them both.

00:06:53.538 --> 00:06:56.040
Betty would later describe
a saucer-shaped craft

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:58.042
with flashing
multi-colored lights

00:06:58.042 --> 00:06:59.961
moving jerkily
through the sky.

00:06:59.961 --> 00:07:03.798
The duo jumped in their car
again to pursue the phenomenon.

00:07:03.798 --> 00:07:05.883
It suddenly came closer--

00:07:05.883 --> 00:07:07.677
much closer--

00:07:07.677 --> 00:07:10.179
hovering over them
in the middle of the highway.

00:07:10.179 --> 00:07:13.266
Barney emerged,
gun and binoculars in hand.

00:07:13.266 --> 00:07:15.810
The pancake-like craft
had a window,

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:19.605
and Barney could see at least
half a dozen figures inside.

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:21.399
They began to emerge.

00:07:21.399 --> 00:07:24.861
Gray in color, human-like,
but smaller in stature

00:07:24.861 --> 00:07:26.696
and with massive eyes,

00:07:26.696 --> 00:07:29.282
the creatures were accompanied
by a buzzing sound.

00:07:29.282 --> 00:07:31.868
Barney and Betty
entered a trance state.

00:07:31.868 --> 00:07:33.703
When they returned
to consciousness,

00:07:33.703 --> 00:07:35.955
seated in the car
two hours later,

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:37.915
56 kilometers away,

00:07:37.915 --> 00:07:40.084
neither could remember
where they had been

00:07:40.084 --> 00:07:41.836
or what had happened.

00:07:41.836 --> 00:07:44.839
They concluded they
had been abducted by aliens.

00:07:44.839 --> 00:07:46.424
Their experience
became the first

00:07:46.424 --> 00:07:48.885
widely publicized
alien abduction.

00:07:48.885 --> 00:07:51.095
The next morning,
a few unusual things

00:07:51.095 --> 00:07:53.014
seemed to confirm
their suspicion.

00:07:53.014 --> 00:07:54.807
Their watches were stopped;

00:07:54.807 --> 00:07:57.727
a pink, powdery substance
stained Betty's dress;

00:07:57.727 --> 00:07:59.770
the binocular straps
were broken;

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:02.815
and circular indents adorned
the trunk of their car.

00:08:02.815 --> 00:08:05.318
Days later,
Betty would report vivid dreams

00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:07.987
that filled in the details
of their lost time.

00:08:07.987 --> 00:08:10.615
In the dreams, the couple
was taken aboard the craft,

00:08:10.615 --> 00:08:12.575
physically examined in detail,

00:08:12.575 --> 00:08:15.620
and questioned telepathically
by the extraterrestrials.

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:17.371
It wasn't
until three years later

00:08:17.371 --> 00:08:19.248
that they took their story
public,

00:08:19.248 --> 00:08:22.501
first to a UFO study group,
and then a month later,

00:08:22.501 --> 00:08:25.338
to seek the help
of a hypnotherapist.

00:08:25.338 --> 00:08:27.423
He concluded that their
experience was a result

00:08:27.423 --> 00:08:29.383
of Betty sharing her dreams,

00:08:29.383 --> 00:08:31.427
not an actual
alien abduction.

00:08:31.427 --> 00:08:33.262
The Hills eventually
reported the incident

00:08:33.262 --> 00:08:36.432
to the U.S. Air Force,
who basically ignored it.

00:08:36.432 --> 00:08:39.477
The National Investigations
Committee on Aerial Phenomenon,

00:08:39.477 --> 00:08:41.771
however,
found the story plausible.

00:08:41.771 --> 00:08:44.398
Following Vilas-Boas'
and the Hills' reports,

00:08:44.398 --> 00:08:46.776
human extraterrestrial
encounters took on

00:08:46.776 --> 00:08:48.569
a rather specific formula--

00:08:48.569 --> 00:08:50.988
a person is taken,
usually against their will,

00:08:50.988 --> 00:08:53.407
onto an alien craft
where they experience

00:08:53.407 --> 00:08:55.576
a traumatic
physical examination

00:08:55.576 --> 00:08:57.995
which includes
the reproductive system

00:08:57.995 --> 00:09:00.414
in what would
come to be known as "probing."

00:09:00.414 --> 00:09:04.085
Sexual activity between humans
and non-humans may occur.

00:09:04.085 --> 00:09:05.836
The person is then returned

00:09:05.836 --> 00:09:09.215
with only a fragmented or
partial memory of the events.

00:09:09.215 --> 00:09:12.301
These experiences seemed
ripped from pulp novels

00:09:12.301 --> 00:09:14.095
and movie screens of the time

00:09:14.095 --> 00:09:16.347
and gained
more and more notoriety

00:09:16.347 --> 00:09:20.309
as they were told and retold
in both fiction and nonfiction.

00:09:20.309 --> 00:09:22.228
Today, may scholars
have connected

00:09:22.228 --> 00:09:24.981
the Hills' abduction story
and its popularity

00:09:24.981 --> 00:09:26.649
to racial anxiety.

00:09:26.649 --> 00:09:28.567
Betty and Barney
were an interracial couple

00:09:28.567 --> 00:09:30.069
and active members

00:09:30.069 --> 00:09:32.154
of the New Hampshire
Civil Rights Movement,

00:09:32.154 --> 00:09:34.991
and by their own account,
the aliens were fascinated

00:09:34.991 --> 00:09:37.034
by their differences
in skin color.

00:09:37.034 --> 00:09:39.453
Apparently, so was
the American public.

00:09:39.453 --> 00:09:41.789
John G. Fuller wrote a book
about the Hill abduction

00:09:41.789 --> 00:09:43.624
in 1966.

00:09:43.624 --> 00:09:46.627
"The Interrupted Journey" was
commercially successful enough

00:09:46.627 --> 00:09:49.880
that it inspired a 1975
film adaptation,

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:51.591
"The UFO Incident."

00:09:51.591 --> 00:09:53.467
That same year in Arizona,

00:09:53.467 --> 00:09:55.886
Travis Walton reported
an abduction incident

00:09:55.886 --> 00:09:59.682
almost exactly like the one
experienced by the Hills

00:09:59.682 --> 00:10:02.184
just two weeks after
"The UFO Incident"

00:10:02.184 --> 00:10:04.061
aired on television.

00:10:04.061 --> 00:10:05.938
Hill would record
his experience

00:10:05.938 --> 00:10:07.565
in the book,
"Fire in the Sky,"

00:10:07.565 --> 00:10:09.692
which also became a film.

00:10:09.692 --> 00:10:12.153
Accounts
of alien abductions spiked

00:10:12.153 --> 00:10:13.696
in conjunction with an increase

00:10:13.696 --> 00:10:16.407
in extraterrestrial encounters
onscreen,

00:10:16.407 --> 00:10:18.743
continuing a cycle of fiction
imitating life

00:10:18.743 --> 00:10:20.453
imitating fiction.

00:10:20.453 --> 00:10:23.247
The appearance of Grays
was solidified and popularized

00:10:23.247 --> 00:10:25.750
in 1977
with Steven Spielberg's

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:27.877
"Close Encounters
of the Third Kind"

00:10:27.877 --> 00:10:30.171
and again in 1988
with the cover art

00:10:30.171 --> 00:10:32.798
of Whitley Strieber's
true-life alien encounters

00:10:32.798 --> 00:10:34.967
science-fiction book
"Communion."

00:10:34.967 --> 00:10:37.386
Almost 40 years later,
in 1980,

00:10:37.386 --> 00:10:39.513
"The Roswell Incident"
was published,

00:10:39.513 --> 00:10:42.308
reigniting the belief
that the 1947 crash

00:10:42.308 --> 00:10:46.312
was evidence of aliens on Earth
and a government cover-up.

00:10:46.312 --> 00:10:48.647
And in 1989,
"Unsolved Mysteries"

00:10:48.647 --> 00:10:51.067
aired a so-called
investigative report

00:10:51.067 --> 00:10:53.486
into the rumored
extraterrestrial activity

00:10:53.486 --> 00:10:57.698
in Roswell
to 28 million viewers.

00:10:57.698 --> 00:11:00.910
The 1990s brought a veritable
golden age of alien abductions

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:02.453
in popular culture.

00:11:02.453 --> 00:11:04.038
To better understand
the community

00:11:04.038 --> 00:11:06.374
that has arisen
around this subject of aliens,

00:11:06.374 --> 00:11:07.875
I asked for some help

00:11:07.875 --> 00:11:09.752
from "Subcultured's"
Josef Lorenzo,

00:11:09.752 --> 00:11:11.545
who recently took a deep dive

00:11:11.545 --> 00:11:13.923
into the UFO
enthusiast community.

00:11:13.923 --> 00:11:15.925
I've been using
the word "enthusiast"

00:11:15.925 --> 00:11:17.426
to describe the community

00:11:17.426 --> 00:11:19.845
because not everyone
is a believer.

00:11:19.845 --> 00:11:21.889
Some people that are
in the community

00:11:21.889 --> 00:11:23.974
are skeptics;
other people are believers.

00:11:23.974 --> 00:11:27.061
And so I've been using
the word "enthusiast"

00:11:27.061 --> 00:11:29.397
to kind of describe
the community as a whole

00:11:29.397 --> 00:11:30.773
because they do come together--

00:11:30.773 --> 00:11:33.567
they have this one
common goal,

00:11:33.567 --> 00:11:36.487
and that goal is that
they want more information.

00:11:36.487 --> 00:11:38.781
There's a big
pop-culture element

00:11:38.781 --> 00:11:40.533
of people's interest
in UFOs

00:11:40.533 --> 00:11:42.493
and UAPs, and I think
a lot of that

00:11:42.493 --> 00:11:44.537
goes to "The X-Files."

00:11:44.537 --> 00:11:46.497
Like, "The X-Files" obviously
was huge in the '90s.

00:11:46.497 --> 00:11:48.916
Everyone was crushing
over Scully and Mulder,

00:11:48.916 --> 00:11:51.377
and it was like
this huge resurgence.

00:11:51.377 --> 00:11:54.255
So there has been this,
like, growing interest

00:11:54.255 --> 00:11:56.590
in aliens
as an aesthetic.

00:11:56.590 --> 00:11:59.468
But I do think that
there is this reality

00:11:59.468 --> 00:12:02.054
that people are just also
interested in aliens

00:12:02.054 --> 00:12:04.890
as, like, a real thing too,
not just an aesthetic.

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:07.726
It's kind of like
an underlying cause for that.

00:12:07.726 --> 00:12:09.520
(Emily)
The Hill abduction inspired
an episode

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:12.898
of "The X-Files" and NBC's
"Dark Skies" series.

00:12:12.898 --> 00:12:16.235
Carl Sagan even discussed it
on his "Cosmos" show.

00:12:16.235 --> 00:12:19.113
Books, including academic ones,
abounded.

00:12:19.113 --> 00:12:22.575
Reputable newspapers wrote
stories of reported abductions.

00:12:22.575 --> 00:12:24.493
Tabloid front pages,
TV shows,

00:12:24.493 --> 00:12:27.705
radio programs--everyone
wanted in on the trend.

00:12:27.705 --> 00:12:30.332
Hollywood blockbusters
like "Independence Day,"

00:12:30.332 --> 00:12:32.668
"Fire in the Sky,"
"Progeny," "Contact,"

00:12:32.668 --> 00:12:35.045
"Mars Attacks," and
"Men in Black" to name a few

00:12:35.045 --> 00:12:38.174
likewise profited
off our alien obsession.

00:12:38.174 --> 00:12:40.301
Since the mid-20th century,
there have been

00:12:40.301 --> 00:12:43.387
four million reports
of alien abductions

00:12:43.387 --> 00:12:45.181
in the U.S. alone.

00:12:45.181 --> 00:12:47.475
The biggest thing
that kind of happened

00:12:47.475 --> 00:12:49.351
for the community was that,

00:12:49.351 --> 00:12:53.063
in 2017, when that "New York
Times" report came out

00:12:53.063 --> 00:12:56.442
admitting that the Pentagon
had a secret program

00:12:56.442 --> 00:12:59.278
that has been
looking into UAPs.

00:12:59.278 --> 00:13:01.447
The one thing that I think
is really significant

00:13:01.447 --> 00:13:03.532
about this last, like, 20 years

00:13:03.532 --> 00:13:08.329
is that if you--
Gallup did a poll in 2005.

00:13:08.329 --> 00:13:11.665
They found that 24%
of people in the United States

00:13:11.665 --> 00:13:14.460
believe that extraterrestrials
have visited Earth.

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:17.463
And when Gallup
did the same poll in 2021,

00:13:17.463 --> 00:13:19.632
they asked people
if these UFOs--

00:13:19.632 --> 00:13:21.884
this footage that has
been released by the Pentagon

00:13:21.884 --> 00:13:24.428
is evidence of intelligent life
outside of Earth,

00:13:24.428 --> 00:13:28.766
51% of people said that
they believed it was.

00:13:28.766 --> 00:13:31.060
This staggering number
could be explained

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:33.062
by the desire for money
or fame.

00:13:33.062 --> 00:13:35.481
Some people have used abduction
as a justification

00:13:35.481 --> 00:13:37.358
for sudden absences at home,

00:13:37.358 --> 00:13:39.276
covering for
an extramarital affair

00:13:39.276 --> 00:13:41.987
or a particularly raucous
night out.

00:13:41.987 --> 00:13:44.114
Psychologists have debated
in the influence

00:13:44.114 --> 00:13:45.533
of false memories--

00:13:45.533 --> 00:13:47.743
a scientifically
proven occurrence

00:13:47.743 --> 00:13:50.412
where memories of incidents
that never occurred

00:13:50.412 --> 00:13:53.707
are implanted into consciousness
with suggestive questioning

00:13:53.707 --> 00:13:56.210
and distortion
of real-world events.

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:59.463
Sleep paralysis is another
proposed explanation.

00:13:59.463 --> 00:14:01.507
Many people report
that their abductions

00:14:01.507 --> 00:14:03.676
occurred at night
in their bedrooms

00:14:03.676 --> 00:14:05.511
where the person
is startled awake

00:14:05.511 --> 00:14:07.763
to find the aliens
at their bedside.

00:14:07.763 --> 00:14:10.849
Sleep paralysis is often
accompanied by auditory

00:14:10.849 --> 00:14:12.643
or visual hallucinations

00:14:12.643 --> 00:14:14.937
as well as temporary
body paralysis.

00:14:14.937 --> 00:14:17.439
Then there are comets
and asteroids to consider,

00:14:17.439 --> 00:14:19.358
as well as
atmospheric phenomenon

00:14:19.358 --> 00:14:21.986
like ball lightning
or St. Elmo's Fire.

00:14:21.986 --> 00:14:24.071
Hoaxes could be
another cause.

00:14:24.071 --> 00:14:26.532
But still, many people swear

00:14:26.532 --> 00:14:29.493
that real contact between
humans and extraterrestrials

00:14:29.493 --> 00:14:30.953
has occurred.

00:14:30.953 --> 00:14:33.622
This might sound silly,
but I like to say

00:14:33.622 --> 00:14:36.125
that the level that you believe
is also a spectrum.

00:14:36.125 --> 00:14:38.544
You know, we talk about
gender and sexuality

00:14:38.544 --> 00:14:39.920
being a spectrum,

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:41.672
but there is a huge spectrum
of people

00:14:41.672 --> 00:14:45.676
who believe things--
the aliens are already here;

00:14:45.676 --> 00:14:48.846
they are reptilians;

00:14:48.846 --> 00:14:50.681
they have all these
different depictions.

00:14:50.681 --> 00:14:53.851
And that goes to just like,
okay, UFOs have been here before

00:14:53.851 --> 00:14:55.728
and those are extraterrestrials.

00:14:55.728 --> 00:14:58.105
No indisputable evidence
has ever been produced

00:14:58.105 --> 00:14:59.940
from an alien abduction--

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:02.192
no objects,
hybrid offspring,

00:15:02.192 --> 00:15:04.862
devices,
or even photographic evidence.

00:15:04.862 --> 00:15:07.406
But that doesn't mean
people have stopped believing

00:15:07.406 --> 00:15:08.866
in extraterrestrial life.

00:15:08.866 --> 00:15:10.200
Quite the opposite.

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:12.786
Then that goes to,
"These are UFOs.

00:15:12.786 --> 00:15:14.622
Maybe they're
extraterrestrials?"

00:15:14.622 --> 00:15:16.457
And it goes to skeptics
that are like,

00:15:16.457 --> 00:15:18.667
"No, this is all a sham,"

00:15:18.667 --> 00:15:20.961
or "This is all just
the government" or whatever.

00:15:20.961 --> 00:15:23.756
So there's this big spectrum
of people

00:15:23.756 --> 00:15:25.299
that are in this community

00:15:25.299 --> 00:15:27.009
that all believe
different things.

00:15:27.009 --> 00:15:29.136
And it creates
a lot of division,

00:15:29.136 --> 00:15:30.471
a lot of drama.

00:15:30.471 --> 00:15:32.181
People get really,
really emotional

00:15:32.181 --> 00:15:35.768
about where they stand
and where other people stand.

00:15:35.768 --> 00:15:37.853
We've seen more varied
interpretations

00:15:37.853 --> 00:15:40.731
of extraterrestrial life
in the 21st century.

00:15:40.731 --> 00:15:42.524
As our knowledge grows,

00:15:42.524 --> 00:15:45.277
we've expanded the concept
of extraterrestrial life

00:15:45.277 --> 00:15:47.279
past green Martians
and Grays

00:15:47.279 --> 00:15:48.989
to sentient beings
that come to Earth

00:15:48.989 --> 00:15:50.783
to share their knowledge.

00:15:50.783 --> 00:15:52.493
As science and technology
advances

00:15:52.493 --> 00:15:55.120
and our understanding
of the universe expands,

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:58.791
our conception of what
constitutes life does as well.

00:15:58.791 --> 00:16:01.543
Science fiction helps us
imagine the philosophical,

00:16:01.543 --> 00:16:03.754
practical,
and moral implications

00:16:03.754 --> 00:16:06.674
of real encounters
between aliens and humans--

00:16:06.674 --> 00:16:09.635
an intellectual testing ground
cloaked in the trappings

00:16:09.635 --> 00:16:11.970
of fantasy to make it
more digestible.

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:14.723
And in exploring
these hypothetical scenarios,

00:16:14.723 --> 00:16:17.726
we question what it means
to be human.

00:16:17.726 --> 00:16:20.312
In other words,
how we conceptualize aliens

00:16:20.312 --> 00:16:22.981
in science fiction
is often more about us

00:16:22.981 --> 00:16:24.775
than it is about them.

00:16:26.485 --> 00:16:28.237
I keep saying
"Euro-peein'."

00:16:28.237 --> 00:16:29.697
(speaker)
European, yep.

00:16:29.697 --> 00:16:31.573
[sighs]

00:16:31.573 --> 00:16:33.325
Cool!

00:16:31.573 --> 00:16:33.325
Rolling.

00:16:33.325 --> 00:16:34.827
"Monstrum" intro.

